{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Righteous</b> — If someone objects: why does He feed one wheat and another barley? The answer is: for He knows what is good for them, for He created them and knows their nature, like a physician who prescribes that each person eat what is good for him. Furthermore: all that HaShem gives is by way of kindness, for there is no obligation upon Him. Therefore: <b>and devout in all His deeds</b>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 145, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:55.217727246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}